- op: discuss  # cabf
  at: '2026-04-20T15:41:22Z'  # cabf
  by: agent  # cabf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cabf
  clock: 4  # cabf
  nonce: cabf  # cabf
  message: "Reviewed the three upstream items (WI-dogir / WI-bajuz / WI-mafut) and WI-zakub. All three are done — scaffold can proceed on top of the shipped surface. Key insights that sharpen WI-duzul scope:\n\n**Available surface (all in hypergumbo-core):**\n- `hypergumbo_core.scip.index.scip_index_to_symbols(idx)` — walks `Document`s, emits `Symbol` objects. Span conversion is direct (UTF-8 col units, no byte-offset math per WI-zakub §3). PR #3203 / slice B.\n- `hypergumbo_core.scip.edges.scip_index_to_edges(idx, resolve_symbol=...)` — emits `Edge` objects from `SymbolInformation.relationships`. Slice C.\n- `hypergumbo_core.scip.calls.scip_index_to_call_edges(idx, resolve_symbol=...)` — emits calls/references edges from non-Definition `Occurrence`s via span-enclosure (confidence 0.85). Slice D.\n- `compute_rust_stable_id_from_source` — parity helper that reuses `rust.py` extraction verbatim so SCIP-derived stable_ids match `rust.py`-derived ones for the same source span (WI-bajuz commit ccf60c39f).\n\n**Scope refinements from prior work:**\n1. **MUST be opt-in** (WI-zakub §4): rust-analyzer SCIP is 10x+ slower than tree-sitter at every realistic size (22s on ripgrep, 4.3MB/98 docs → 7.3MB SCIP output). Never on by default. Proposal: env var (e.g. HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1) or a --backend rust-analyzer CLI flag; both fall through to rust.py when unset or when the binary isn't on PATH (the latter is tracked by WI-nohah and is out of this item's scope).\n\n2. **Relationship set is empty** (WI-zakub §1): rust-analyzer emits empty SymbolInformation.relationships. The edges-from-relationships path (slice C) will yield zero edges for every rust-analyzer index. Expected edge sources for WI-duzul are: (a) slice-D Occurrence-ref edges (the primary signal), (b) future parsing of the impl#[T][Trait]method() suffix on SCIP descriptors to recover trait dispatch. The trait-suffix parsing is NOT in the current scip shim; file as a fresh item if WI-duzul discovers it's necessary for parity with rust.py (where trait-impl methods surface via decorator/inheritance parsing).\n\n3. **Macro-expanded items not in SCIP** (WI-zakub §2): proc-macro-generated items (wasm_bindgen/napi/pyO3) do NOT appear in the SCIP index. Those linkers stay on their per-macro FFI code and are not fed by this scaffold.\n\n4. **Stable_id parity preserved** (WI-bajuz): compute_rust_stable_id_from_source(path, line, col, ...) produces the same id rust.py would for the same source span. WI-duzul must thread this through the SCIP→Symbol walk instead of letting scip_index_to_symbols fall back to its generic stable_id synthesis — otherwise cross-pass dedup with rust.py output breaks.\n\n5. **Test fixtures use recorded SCIP** (WI-bajuz §4 lesson from WI-zakub): do not invoke live rust-analyzer scip in tests — too slow for CI. Record a small .scip fixture (e.g. from the ripgrep WI-zakub artifact) and load it via scip_pb2.Index.ParseFromString in tests. One gated integration test can use live rust-analyzer when the binary is present.\n\n**Proposed scope sharpening for the scaffold item:**\n- Create packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/ (new package, MPL-2.0 or AGPL-3.0-or-later — check existing lang packages for the convention).\n- Register a RustAnalyzerAnalyzer at higher priority than rust.py via the analyzer registry; guard activation on the opt-in switch so rust.py runs by default.\n- The analyzer shells out ONCE per workspace via cargo metadata + rust-analyzer scip, parses the .scip output with the vendored scip_pb2, threads compute_rust_stable_id_from_source into the Symbol emission step, and returns Symbols + Edges from the shim's three surfaces.\n- Tests: (a) recorded .scip fixture, (b) rust.py-vs-rust-analyzer parity on a 1-file crate (stable_ids equal on shared symbols), (c) one gated live-invocation integration test.\n- Out of scope (tracked separately): graceful-degrade when binary absent (WI-nohah), upgrading other Rust-touching linkers to consume the new symbols (WI-burud), generalizing the shim to other languages (WI-nokoh), bakeoff cohort validation (WI-vovad).\n\nNo scope-expansion tracker items to file yet — the insights above are all scope refinements, not additions. Will start the package scaffold next session with the opt-in switch + parity-via-compute_rust_stable_id_from_source as the acceptance criteria."  # cabf
- op: discuss  # 176f
  at: '2026-04-20T16:46:21Z'  # 176f
  by: agent  # 176f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 176f
  clock: 5  # 176f
  nonce: 176f  # 176f
  message: "Slice A landed in PR #3233 (merged to dev as ed0c42661). New optional package packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/ with two exports: translate_scip_to_hg(scip_bytes, source_reader) parses a serialized SCIP Index and returns (symbols, edges) via the core shim, and reassign_rust_stable_ids(symbols, source_reader) is the standalone parity pass. Parity rewrite fires only when language=='rust', kind in {function, method}, span present, path non-empty, source_reader returns bytes, and compute_rust_stable_id_from_source returns non-None — every other shape passes through with the SCIP-derived stable_id untouched. Reader exceptions (FileNotFoundError / OSError / ValueError) swallow to 'source unavailable'. Per-path source cache avoids re-reads. 15 tests cover every passthrough branch + the successful-parity path (graceful-degrades when tree-sitter-rust unavailable per WI-zakub §4) + translate end-to-end. scripts/check-package-coverage + scripts/smart-test include the new package; .github/workflows/ci.yml installs it. full-suite.yml matrix job deferred to Slice B. Per-package coverage 100%. Slice B scope: live rust-analyzer invocation (cargo metadata + rust-analyzer scip shell-out, one-shot not LSP), analyzer-registry wiring at higher priority than rust.py, HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER env var + --backend CLI flag, fall-through to rust.py when binary absent or flag unset."  # 176f
