- op: discuss  # 19f1
  at: '2026-04-20T21:18:21Z'  # 19f1
  by: agent  # 19f1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 19f1
  clock: 11  # 19f1
  nonce: 19f1  # 19f1
  message: "Slice C-final shipped (merged to dev as 544d86983). New hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer.analyzer.analyze_rust_with_scip @register_analyzer('rust_analyzer', priority=45) with entry-point registration so the SCIP pass dispatches through the hypergumbo-core registry alongside rust.py (priority 50 default). Gate False → empty AnalysisResult (no file walk, no subprocess); gate True → try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer + None-to-empty mapping for graceful-degrade. SCIP Symbols carry origin='scip' for trust-weighting. 7 new tests, 100% coverage. Env-var activation (HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1) works today; --backend CLI flag parsing remains deferred (tracked as a small follow-up if needed — the analyzer primitive is ready to consume it).\n\nFull WI-duzul stack delivered:\n- Slice A: translate_scip_to_hg (PR #3233)\n- Slice B-first: run_rust_analyzer_scip shell-out (PR #3234)\n- Slice C gate: should_use_rust_analyzer_backend (PR #3242)\n- Slice C-final: registered analyzer (this slice)\n\nParallel infrastructure shipped alongside:\n- WI-dotud: install-rust-analyzer subcommand (PR #3236)\n- WI-huham: install-extras umbrella (PR #3237)\n- WI-nohah: graceful-degrade orchestrator (4ebcf0f79)\n\nTagging awaits_bakeoff_validation — the backend should improve Rust-heavy corpus coverage (concrete-impl trait dispatch, cross-crate refs) once activated via opt-in. Validation requires a DEEP cycle with HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 on a Rust-heavy repo."  # 19f1
